          "title": "You'll want to know: فضول",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "فضول — fuzūl — \"pointless, wasteful\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "فضول (fuzūl) is a loan from Arabic fuḍūl, \"excesses, what is left over\", which reached Urdu through Persian. Its Arabic root is f-ḍ-l (Lane). It is the plural of faḍl, \"excess\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
